; Hullbreach: hold three broken space stations against waves of machines, with four guns and a lot of jumping.
;
; Every picture and sound in this game is made by the code itself, so there are no files to ship with it.
;
; Controls:
;   Mouse                  look around
;   W A S D                run
;   Space                  jump (hold it to keep jumping when you land)
;   Left mouse button      fire (hold it to keep firing)
;   1 2 3 4, mouse wheel   choose a gun
;   Escape or P            the pause menu
;   Menus                  Up/Down or the mouse choose, Enter/Space or a click select, Left/Right change an option
;
; How it plays: every station is one arena, floating in space. The machines come in four waves per station, and the
; last wave of the last station brings the Warden. Health, armour and ammunition lie at fixed places and come back
; a while after they are taken, so it pays to learn where they are. The edges of the stations are open: whoever falls
; off drops into space, the machines too. Rockets push you around, so a rocket fired at your feet throws you up high.
;
; How it works: the arenas are lists of boxes and ramps in Data lines, made into one mesh. The player and the walking
; machines are ellipsoids that slide along that mesh with Blitz3D's own collisions (Collisions, UpdateWorld). Guns
; that hit at once (the scattergun and the railgun) trace a line: LinePick finds the wall it stops at, and a little
; sphere test finds the machines in front of that wall. Everything slower is a shot that moves a bit every update.
;
; The options and the best score are saved in hullbreach.cfg next to the program.

